brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net can you build a MegaHAL website so we can talk to MegaHAL? that would be fun. maybe with a dropdown for the different brains, like default, aliens, ferris, etc.. i found a repo at github.com/kranzky/mega..., maybe make that work in a website somehow. we believe in you!

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@gracekind.net: You’ll never guess who released research on this

https://alignment.openai.com/self-incrimination/
  [quoting @shimmermathlabs.com: 'confess' tool call so agents can make mistakes, confess their sins, and keep going]
  [image, alt text: Training agents to self-report misbehavior

Mar 21, 2026 · Bruce W. Lee, Yueh-Han Chen and Tomek Korbak
TL;DR We train agents to call a report_scheming() tool when they covertly misbehave. Self-incrimination reduces undetected successful attacks]
@chbarts.bsky.social: Some of my great-grandparents went from flying being a novelty to seeing people walk on the Moon. I don't know what went through their heads when the world went from voice on radio being new to TV from the Moon, but I'm feeling something that must be similar about AI now. I remember ELIZA, dammit.
@chbarts.bsky.social: MegaHAL won the Loebner Prize and now I could probably get Claude to write a MegaHAL clone with a single prompt.
